304:### Prioritize (page 4)
305-Page 4 continues on page 3's car in the same canvas: the requirement pins lift off the car and become a priority skyline around it (D-050). Unit = requirement × car line × market.
306-- **Transition:** each pin leaves its zone on a lifted arc to its slot on a ring around the car (radius ≈ 1.4 × the car's half-length), then grows up into its column; the columns leave in ring order, about 2.3 s in all. The car stays solid (no x-ray); the skyline stands on the ring around it. Going back to Definition runs the same move in reverse: the columns shrink, fly back onto their zones, and page 3's pins take over once they have landed (page 3 stays on its last stage, no replay). Under reduced motion every move jumps.
307-- **Skyline:** one column per requirement on the car line, grouped by vehicle domain round the ring (a gap between groups, the group's name and count as a ground chip outside it), ordered by best score; every requirement keeps its slot across markets. Height = the target's score in the selected market (100 ≈ twice the car's height). Hue = domain; band = mark: Must a solid square column, Should an outlined column over a 13% fill, Could a thin line with a cap dot. A market without a target leaves a hollow ink-3 slot on the ground. The score sits above each column as a small wide numeral on a 62% black chip (colliding chips hide, lowest score first); Must numerals in ink, the rest ink-2.
308-- **Thresholds:** two faint planes over the ring at Should 45 and Must 60: a white annulus at ~3–4% plus hairline circles, each named in micro caps on the camera side.
309-- **Market switch:** the heights morph (≈ 0.6 s ease) and the marks change band in place, so the PM sees where markets disagree (D-011). `[` / `]` step through the line's markets.
310-- **JAN → JUL:** a ghost tick (white, 38%) keeps JAN's height; the numeral adds the delta; risers and fallers (≥ 3 points or a band change) send out one white ring; an open AI proposal adds a ▲ / ▼ to the numeral.
311-- **Bundles and flags:** a bundle's bases are joined by a faint white chord through the inside of the ring (16%, 62% while a member is hovered or open, or "Show bundle"). Two Musts that must be chosen jointly carry a dashed white arc between their tops, labelled "choose jointly · <resource>" in the dashed link tag. Brand-fit fail puts a barred ink circle before the numeral.
312-- **The PM's position:** a confirmed band is the one blue mark: a sweep-hi disc with its wash halo at the column's base; in DOM, a sweep-hi underline with the wash under the band mark and the blue "PM" tag.
313-- **Attention:** hovered and open columns turn white (the open one's numeral gets a 1px white ring); opening one dims the others to 28%; the camera glides so the ring sits left of the panel.
314-- **Top-left (below the page switch):** the band readout (Must / Should / Could as 34px numerals with their band mark), a hairline, then Proposals, Choose jointly, Blocked and Markets disagree at 20px; a micro line (targets, PM-confirmed, weights scheme, "market weight stylized (Q-015)"); the car line, market and Skyline / Matrix switches as segmented pills; the dashed "Sample data" note while the stage has not run.
315-- **Priorities pill:** top-right next to Audit (one panel at a time). With nothing open, the ranked list for the market grouped by band: rank, band mark (domain hue), title, tags (PM, barred brand circle, dashed "joint", "→ band" for a proposal), confidence level, score with ▲▼ since JAN.
316-- **Inspector:** domain · line · market; title; the score at 52px with the band, "PM" or "AI proposal", rank and confidence; the same requirement in the line's other markets as small buttons (band mark + score; "markets disagree"); the waterfall; rationale on a rail; gates (pass a filled dot, warn a half-filled ring, fail a barred ring, with the checker's reason; brand fail adds the blocking line); the ladder rung with a what-if switch (baseline / threshold / target / stretch: the recomputed score, band change and "+1 exposure via <resource>" for linked requirements, never stored); bundle members; flags; history per checkpoint; an open proposal (old → proposed band, cause, factor deltas, Accept / Reject with a required rationale); the PM decision (Must / Should / Could as band-mark buttons, "AI" on the proposed one, required rationale, "Override and confirm" when brand fit fails).
317-- **Waterfall (D-037):** one 0–100 scale, rows grouped Customer / Business / Future: each factor a step from the running total (ink-2), a missing factor a dashed "gap" box; the base as an outlined bar; × confidence and negative modifiers as ink-3 hatched steps down; the score as a full ink bar; Should 45 and Must 60 as dashed vertical lines named above, and a white "what-if" tick while a rung is previewed. Neutral only.
318-- **Matrix:** the 2D alternative, on the inspector's field between the left column and the right panel: rows grouped by domain, one column per market of the line (the selected one outlined); each cell the band mark in the domain hue with its score, ▲▼ where JAN → JUL moved it, "P" for an open proposal, the PM underline where confirmed; a white tick at the row's end where markets disagree. Clicking a cell opens that market's target. The skyline behind steps back (columns 28%, labels 12%). Esc returns to the skyline.
319-- **Guide / Agent:** the dock's Guide explains the skyline with its own marks (or the matrix, or the open target's waterfall); the Agent panel shows the page-4 stages (fit gate, score).
