321-## Do's and Don'ts
322-
323-### Do:
324-- **Do** keep the ground pure black (#000) and render overlays as blurred glass over the live canvas.
325-- **Do** give each raw data type its own categorical hue and repeat that hue in its legend glyph wherever the type is named.
326-- **Do** encode track state by mark shape: dot = held, ring = acquired by this sweep. The direction reserves double ring = strengthened and amber cross = lost for the clustering stage on; those marks are not built yet, so record them here once they ship.
327-- **Do** set every count as a wide (118%), light (300), tabular numeral and keep its label at micro size.
328-- **Do** play the sweep once on arrival and once per checkpoint change, using cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1) for UI motion (160ms for colour, 240ms for panels and nodes).
329-- **Do** give every element in the volume an inspector that names its layer and says in one line what it encodes.
330-- **Do** honour reduced motion: transitions and animations drop to 0ms. The one exception is the focus glide (opening an item lifts its layer and sinks the others): it still glides without overshoot, pulse or ripple, because the move is what shows which layer the item belongs to.
331-
332-### Don't:
333-- **Don't** auto-rotate the volume or add idle motion; it moves only when the PM drags it.
334-- **Don't** use sweep blue for data, hover or decoration; it belongs to the sweep and the PM's position.
335-- **Don't** use amber for anything but weakened or lost tracks and lost signal, and never without its cross mark.
336-- **Don't** frame evidence in sidebar-plus-chart-card dashboards or opaque panels; overlays float at the edges of the volume.
337-- **Don't** set text below ink-3 (#868d99) on black.
338-- **Don't** write paragraph copy in the interface; paragraphs belong to the evidence itself.

